w: 2.~The Lord God his sal- va- ti- _ on hath caus- _ èd to be known; His jus- tice _ in the hea- then's sight he o- _ pen- ly hath _ shown.
w: 3.~He mind- ful of his grace and _ truth to Is- _ r'el's house hath been; And the sal- _ va- tion of our God all ends _ of th'earth have _ seen.
w: 4.~Let all the earth un- to the _ Lord send forth _ a joy- ful noise; Lift up your _ voice a- loud to him, sing prais- _ es, and re- _ joice.
w: 5.~With harp, with harp, and voice of _ psalms, un- to _ Je- ho- vah sing: With trum- pets, _ cor- nets, glad- ly sound be- fore _ the Lord the _ King.
w: 6.~Let seas and all their full- ness _ roar; the world, _ and dwell- ers there; Let floods clap _ hands, and let the hills to- ge- _ ther joy de- _ clare
w: 7.~Be- fore the Lord; be- cause he _ comes, to judge _ the earth comes he: He'll judge the _ world with right- eous- ness, his folk _ with e- qui- _ ty.
